2 TITL West's Ordinary, Fairfax, Virginia
1 _OID 4bf153cf-93ee-43c1-bc13-4feb33684be8
1 PLAC West's Ordinary, Fairfax, Virginia
1 _DSCR http://lvaimage.lib.va.us/VHI/html/22/0782.html Report Home Page  
2 CONT Morton, Susan R. 
2 CONT survey report, West’s Ordinary (old site) : 1937 Feb. 23 / research made by Susan R. Morton. 
2 CONT 3 leaves. 
2 CONT Map location number: PW62 
2 CONT Class: Tavern (site) 
2 CONT Building date: 1755 
2 CONT Building plan: Rectangular 
2 CONT Number of stories: 2 
2 CONT Building material: Stone 
2 CONT Location: 2 miles southwest of Aldie off Little River Road. 
2 CONT Primary owners: Charles West, Jospeh Lacy family, Riticor 
2 CONT Also known as: Lacy’s Public House 
2 CONT The Little River Road was the major corridor of travel from the county into the Shenandoah Valley and this was a major stopping point for travellers. George Washington was a regular visitor and General Lafayette was entertained here in 1787. It wa
2 CONC s used as a meeting place by locals as well. 
2 CONT Includes description of the ordinary, and site. It was torn down about 1927. 
2 CONT Includes abstracts of title. 
2 CONT Also available on microfilm. 
2 CONT Computer file. Richmond, Va. : Library of Virginia, 1998. 3 image files. 
2 CONT This write-up is a part of the Virginia W.P.A. Historical Inventory Project sponsored by the Virginia Conservation Commission under the direction of its Division of History. 
2 CONT West’s Ordinary (Prince William County, Va.) 
2 CONT Taverns (Inns) -- Virginia -- Prince William County. 
2 CONT Stone buildings -- Virginia -- Prince William County. 
2 CONT Architecture. -- 18th century -- Virginia -- Prince William County. 
2 CONT Prince William County (Va.) -- History, Local. 
2 CONT Prince William County (Va.). -- Social life and customs. 
2 CONT Surveys. 
2 CONT Abstracts of title -- Virginia -- Prince William County. 
2 CONT Ewell, Maud, informant. 
2 CONT 
