2 TITL Descendants of Timothy Rockwood, page 9
1 _OID d8fd5d23-6363-4278-952d-19c74dfe5f6a
1 DATE 10 May 2012
1 PLAC Screenshot
1 _DSCR A Historical and Genealogical Record of the Descendants of Timothy Rockwood (1856), By Elbridge Luther Rockwood - Google EBooks
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription>RECORD.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Samuel Rockwood, the father of Timothy RockWood, whose genealogy is the subject of these pages, was bom in Medfield, Mass., April 15th, 1695, and died in Medway, Jan'y 11th, 1754. *
2 CONT 
2 CONT The Rockwoods, during the last part of the Sixteenth and the first of the Seventeenth Centuries, were called Rockets. Their names were pronounced Rocket and written Rocket in the old records. This Samuel was born a Rocket, lived a Rocket, but die
2 CONC d a Rockwood. There is no evidence, however, that their own signatures were ever written any other way than Rockwood.
2 CONT 
2 CONT A large part of the town of Medway was taken from Medfield, and was not incorporated when this Samuel
2 CONT 
2 CONT * The names of the father and mother of this Samuel, were John Rocket and Bethia. They lived in Medfield. Was this the house of three generations'! See Medfield Town Records.
2 CONT </transcription></metadataxml>
