1 _DSCR The church dates from the Norman Invasion and was extensively damaged by a landmine on 21st September 1940; reconstruction was not complete until 1955. The tower is one of the most notable timber framed towers in Essex, being also the oldest. It wa
2 CONC s constructed in 1370. A moat, a remnant of a defensive earthwork borders the churchyard on the north side of the massive vault of the Waldegrave family.
