2 TITL Hart Family Book
1 _OID ff4db9bb-b718-4145-87a0-acea9719698b
1 _DSCR Birth:  1740
2 CONT South Carolina, USA 
2 CONT Death:  1820
2 CONT Alleghany County
2 CONT North Carolina, USA 
2 CONT 
2 CONT Born ca. 1740 perhaps in PA or the current Northern part of South Carolina, now Mecklenburg County, North Carolina or perhaps Old Montgomery County Virginia.
2 CONT Peter Hart's parents are unknown. However, Peter might be a son or grandson of Thomas the Elder Hart and Ester Miles.
2 CONT Proof is needed.
2 CONT A Peter, John Hart and George Sizemore are listed together on the muster roll of John Hitchcock's company 1759-1760 during the Cherokee expedition to Fort Prince George, South Carolina (one of the Companies of Colonel George Gabriel Powell). 
2 CONT Peter Hart and his brother James Hart both appear on a muster roll of Capt. John Cox's Company in Montgomery County, Virginia in 1781. This record is found in the book "Montgomery County Revolutionary War Records 1775-1783."
2 CONT 
2 CONT "Descendants of Peter and Dority Hart 1740-1995 Virginia and North Carolina and Allied Families" by Ruth Gibbs Hart and Karen L. Cooper
2 CONT 
2 CONT Peter and Dority were the parents of nine children. Many of them left the area for Knox/Whitley County Kentucky, Hawkins County Tennessee and Mercer County Missouri.
2 CONT 1, James Hart born 1768
2 CONT 2, Mark Hart born Abt. 1770, married to Barbara Kirk on September 17, 1800 in Grayson County Virginia.
2 CONT 3, Margaret (Mahala) Hart born Bet. 1772 - 1774, NC, married Abt. 1796 to Stephen Floyd. They lived and died in Whitley/Knox County Kentucky but thier grave sites are unknown.
2 CONT 4, William Hart born Abt. 1775, Montgomery/Grayson CO., VA, married Abt. 1798, VA or NC to Mary Cadwell (Caldwell).
2 CONT 5, Peter Jr Hart born 1780, NC, married Hannah Poe, May 18, 1801, Jefferson, Ashe CO., NC.
2 CONT 6, John Hart born February 20, 1780, Grayson CO., VA, first marriage to Permelia Morgan, Abt. 1800, Grayson.
2 CONT Second marriage, Lydia Rains, May 10, 1827, Whitley County Kentucky. John lived on Meadow Creek, Whitley Co., Kentucky and is buried there with Lydia Rains in Stanfield Cemetery.
2 CONT 7, Nancy Hart born Abt. 1784, Grayson CO., VA, married to Andrew Hash, February 25, 1805, Grayson CO., VA.
2 CONT 8, Stephen Hart born 1785, Montgomery (now Grayson) CO., VA., married to Sarah Bradford, May 30, 1805, Grayson CO., VA.
2 CONT 9, Unknown Son, maybe David Hart born after 1785. 
2 CONT  
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Dority Hart (1745 - 1820)
2 CONT  
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Margaret Hart Floyd (1773 - 1848)*
2 CONT   William Hart (1775 - 1840)*
2 CONT   John Hart (1780 - 1855)*
2 CONT   Peter Hart (1780 - 1842)*
2 CONT   Nancy Hart Hash (1784 - 1855)*
2 CONT   Stephen Hart (1785 - 1870)*
2 CONT  
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT  
2 CONT   
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT Peter Hart Family Cemetery 
2 CONT Alleghany County
2 CONT North Carolina, USA 
2 CONT  
2 CONT Created by: Wes Hart
2 CONT Record added: Oct 05, 2009 
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 42738289 
2 CONT  
2 CONT  
2 CONT 
